course: dictionary
lesson: 5542
title: Legged words and their numbers
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Legged is a word that tells you about legs. It is hardly ever used alone. You usually find it in a pair of words joined by a dash, like four-legged or long-legged. The first part tells you how many legs, or what kind of legs, there are.
explain: «Count the four-legged animals together, then the two-legged ones, and add the two counts of legs.» Four-legged means having four legs, and two-legged means having two legs. The dash joins the words so they work as one describing word.
explain: Look for the clues in the sentence. In science, birds and humans are two-legged, and insects are six-legged. In sports day, a three-legged race means two runners are tied together at the legs. Ask yourself: how many legs is the word talking about?
fact: Legged means having legs.
fact: Legged is usually used in a compound word with a dash, such as four-legged, two-legged or long-legged.
fact: «Four-legged» describes dogs and cats, and a «four-legged friend» means a pet animal.
fact: Insects are six-legged, and spiders are eight-legged.
fact: Informally, «leg it» (or «legged it») means to run away fast.
exercise: «Count the four-legged animals together, then the two-legged ones.» What does four-legged mean? | *Having four legs | Having four wheels | Having four coats of paint | Having four heads
exercise: In a science lesson, which animal is six-legged? | A spider | A human | *An insect | A dog
exercise: Jade says, "We legged it when the bell rang." What does legged it mean? | Sat down slowly | Counted the legs | Had two legs | *Ran away fast
test: Which phrase names a race at sports day? | cross-legged | *three-legged race | bow-legged | four-legged friend
test: Spiders are eight-legged. How many legs does a spider have? | *eight | two | four | six
exam: Which word means having two legs? | four-legged | long-legged | *two-legged | cross-legged
